#
#  The Venus cloud sea, as Cosmos `@media/skybox` labels.
#
#  Six skies, generated by `_gen_skybox.py` rather than painted: every pixel is a pure
#  function of its 3D direction, so all twelve cube edges and both poles are seamless by
#  construction rather than by retouching. See that file for the why.
#
#  ART: media/skybox/venus_sky_*.png, 4096x3072. Not in this mastlib - see __init__.mast.
#
#  THEY ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. The altitude gradient is the mission's most important
#  piece of set dressing, because in this setting DOWN KILLS YOU - the deck is pressure and
#  heat, and the ceiling is air too thin to hold lift. A mission should pick the sky that
#  matches the band it is set in, not roll at random:
#
#      high_haze   the thin bright air at the top of the world
#      midday      the working altitude - the trade lanes
#      dusk        the terminator, long light, the classic Kingdom postcard
#      stormwall   a convective wall; something has gone wrong
#      deep        below the trade lanes, where salvage and pirates live
#      nightside   no sun at all, only the glow of the deck
#
#  MUSIC: none of these touch it. Each label used to end in a two-line body that scheduled
#  random music, because scheduling a skybox runs its body and nothing anywhere else ever
#  chose a track - so an empty body left a game silent. Music is now selected on its own,
#  from the MUSIC_SELECT setting, a map's `Defaults:`, or the server console's dropdown,
#  and a mod supplies a soundtrack by declaring `@media/music/<bank>` - which this one does,
#  at the bottom of this file (the Venus_Clouds bank).
#
#  That matters more here than for most packs: these skies are picked deliberately, per
#  band, and re-rolling the music every time a mission changed the sky was never wanted.
#

@media/skybox/venus_sky_high_haze "Venus - High Haze (pale gold)"

@media/skybox/venus_sky_midday "Venus - Midday Deck (amber)"

@media/skybox/venus_sky_dusk "Venus - Terminator Dusk (orange)"

@media/skybox/venus_sky_stormwall "Venus - Storm Wall (dark umber)"

@media/skybox/venus_sky_deep "Venus - Deep Deck (oppressive)"

@media/skybox/venus_sky_nightside "Venus - Nightside (dim sulfur)"


#
#  The Venus soundtrack, declared as a music bank.
#
#  A `@media/music` label names a BANK - a folder holding start/main/victory/failure.ogg
#  plus low/ medium/ high/ - not a track. `music_get_list()` finds this, so it appears in
#  the server console's Music dropdown, and venus_set_default_music() makes it the mod
#  default (a mission, profile or the command line can still pick another).
#
#  Generated with YuE2 by E:\ai\YuE\venus_soundtrack.bat; CREDITS.txt in the bank lists
#  every track's prompt and seed.
#
#  WHERE THE FILES ARE, and why this may play the stock music for now. The bank travels in
#  this mod's shared-media pack at `media/music/Venus_Clouds`. The ENGINE only accepts a
#  bare folder name under `data/audio/music` for `set_music_folder` - a path hangs it
#  (measured in `missions/music_probe`, engine 1.3.6). So sbs_utils resolves the bank from
#  the pack, declines to hand the engine a path, logs a warning, and plays `default` -
#  unless the folder has also been copied to `data/audio/music/Venus_Clouds`, which the
#  resolver checks first. Flip MUSIC_ENGINE_ACCEPTS_PATHS once the engine is fixed.
#
@media/music/Venus_Clouds "Venus Clouds"
